import lib/geometry.dl

class:
    patterns:
        [a|] spatial camera
    members:
        position as spatial position
        yaw as a floating-point number
        movement as a floating-point number
        turning as a floating-point number

class:
    patterns:
        [a|] spatial bounding box
    members:
        minimum as spatial position
        maximum as spatial position

[a|] spatial position means: the type of (a position with x 0.0, y 0.0 and z 0.0)
[the|] spatial dimensions means: a point
[a|] spatial color means: a color
[a|] normalized color means: a color
a position with x {floating-point number:x}, y {floating-point number:y} and z {floating-point number:z} means: @intrinsic(
    "construct",
    a point,
    @intrinsic("construct", an aggregate of 3 floating-point number values, x, y, z)
)

the dimensions measuring {floating-point number:width} by {floating-point number:height} by {floating-point number:depth} means: @intrinsic(
    "construct",
    a point,
    @intrinsic("construct", an aggregate of 3 floating-point number values, width, height, depth)
)

a color with red {integer:red}, green {integer:green} and blue {integer:blue} means: @intrinsic(
    "construct",
    a color,
    @intrinsic("construct", an aggregate of 3 integer values, red, green, blue)
)

a normalized color with red {floating-point number:red}, green {floating-point number:green} and blue {floating-point number:blue} means: @intrinsic(
    "construct",
    a color,
    @intrinsic("construct", an aggregate of 3 floating-point number values, red, green, blue)
)

a camera at {spatial position:position} facing {floating-point number:yaw} degrees with speed {floating-point number:movement} and turn rate {floating-point number:turning} means: @intrinsic("construct", a spatial camera, position, yaw, movement, turning)
a bounding box from {spatial position:minimum} to {spatial position:maximum} means: @intrinsic("construct", a spatial bounding box, minimum, maximum)
